<h2>Why Multi-Family Roofing Is Different</h2>
<p>A multi-family roof is rarely one roof. It is a collection of rooflines, elevations and sometimes several materials installed in different decades. Add residents, parked cars, landscaping, pools and playgrounds, and the risks multiply. The things that separate a smooth project from a chaotic one are mostly planning:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Consistency across buildings.</strong> Matching shingle color, ridge profile and flashing details so the community looks uniform when it is done.</li>
  <li><strong>Liability and safety.</strong> Falling debris, ladders and dumpsters near occupied units require marked zones and constant cleanup.</li>
  <li><strong>Decision-makers.</strong> Owners, asset managers, boards and on-site staff all need the right information at the right time.</li>
  <li><strong>Budget timing.</strong> Many communities need to spread roof work across fiscal years or reserve cycles.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Our Multi-Family Roof Replacement Process</h2>
<p>Whether you need multi-family roof replacement in Austin for a single building or a phased re-roof of an entire community, the process follows the same structure:</p>
<ol class="steps">
