<h2>New Multi-Family Roof Installation in Austin</h2>
<p>As an Austin multi-family roof installation company, we also work with builders and general contractors on new townhome and apartment projects. Multi-family roof installation in Austin means coordinating with framing, plumbing and HVAC trades, following the plans and local code, and getting each building dried in quickly so interiors can proceed. We focus on the details that cause trouble later on attached housing: firewall and parapet flashing, valleys between units, and attic ventilation in shared spaces.</p>

<h2>Austin Conditions That Shape Multi-Family Roofs</h2>
<p>Central Texas communities face the same weather as single-family homes, multiplied by dozens of roofs. A single spring hailstorm can damage every building on a property at once, and straight-line winds often strip shingles from the most exposed elevations first. Summer heat ages roofs quickly where attics are poorly ventilated — a common issue on older complexes. Large live oaks shading parking lots look great but fill valleys and gutters with leaves, which leads to leaks at the same spots year after year.</p>
<p>Many communities in Williamson and Hays counties also have HOA or deed rules covering roofing color and material, and some boards are moving to impact-resistant (Class 4) shingles to reduce hail claims. We can help you compare options for your community — see our <a href="/services/shingle-roofing/">composition shingle roofing</a> page for the differences.</p>

<div class="callout callout--tip"><p><strong>Hail hit the whole property?</strong> We document each building separately with photos and roof diagrams, which makes it easier for owners and associations to work through an insurance claim. Read how we help on our <a href="/services/roof-insurance-claims/">roof insurance claim help</a> page and in our guide to <a href="/blog/insurance-coverage-for-storm-damaged-roofs/">insurance coverage for storm-damaged roofs</a>.</p></div>

<h2>Maintenance Programs for Communities</h2>
<p>The cheapest roof on a multi-family property is the one that lasts its full design life. A spring and fall inspection program — clearing valleys and gutters, resealing penetrations, replacing lifted shingles and checking low-slope sections — prevents many of the interior leaks that generate work orders and resident complaints. It also gives you documented roof history when it is time to budget for replacement or file a storm claim.</p>
<p>For buildings with flat sections or a mix of commercial and residential space, see our <a href="/services/commercial-roofing/">commercial roofing</a> and <a href="/services/commercial-roof-coatings/">roof coating</a> services.</p>

